# Generated value-vector coverage snapshots.
#
# `pine:value-vectors` writes a coverage artifact on every run. Adjacent
# generations are near-identical -- a 2026-09 audit measured 0 of 931 cases
# changed between consecutive versions -- so committing the series added
# ~570MB of history for no reviewable signal, and it was stripped from the
# branch before merge.
#
# Two snapshots stay TRACKED because scripts import them; gitignore does not
# untrack existing files, so they are unaffected by the rules below:
#   pine-value-vectors-coverage-v117.json
#   pine-value-vectors-coverage-v174.json
#
# TRAP: if a future generation is genuinely needed as a committed input, it
# will be silently ignored here -- the same failure that once kept a real
# source file out of a build because root `.gitignore` carried a bare
# `coverage/`. Stage it deliberately with `git add -f <path>` and say why in
# the commit message.
pine-value-vectors-coverage-v*.json
pine-value-vectors-coverage-v*.md
